If-Else Statements Using Strings

I learned how to use if-else statements to check string input in C programming.

Concepts Covered

How to declare a string using a character array (char).
How to take string input using fgets().
How to use strlen() to calculate the length of a string.
How to remove the newline character (\n) using the null terminator (\0).
How to check whether a string is empty using strlen() == 0.
How to use if-else statements with string conditions.

I created a simple C program that asks the user to enter their name.

If the user leaves the input empty, it displays "You did not enter your name".
If the user enters a name, it displays "Hello" followed by their name.

What I Practiced
String handling
fgets()
strlen()
sizeof()
Null terminator (\0)
If-else statements
Conditional logic

Today's Progress: Learned how to check string input using if-else statements and the strlen() function in C.